nvk: Fermi..Volta block-linear modifier images get no host-visible VRAM type.

On Fermi..Volta a CPU map of host-visible VRAM goes through BAR1, and BAR1
does not return a block-linear DRM-modifier image's bytes in the modifier's
layout, whatever PTE kind the memory carries. Measured on GP104 (closed
kernel module 580.178.04): image filled by the GPU through its own VA, read
back through a BAR1 map: 41040/82080 texels at their block-linear offsets
with a pitch-kind allocation, 2592/82080 with the block-linear kind; through
a system-memory map 82080/82080. On GB202 BAR1 reads back exactly.

The proprietary driver offers no host-visible VRAM type for such images
(580.178.04 Vulkan ICD on GP104: vkGetImageMemoryRequirements memoryTypeBits
0x82 for a 1440x854 R8G8B8A8 image with modifier 0x03000000004fe015, i.e. a
non-host-visible system type and the device-local type). Do the same before
Turing: drop the DEVICE_LOCAL|HOST_VISIBLE types from memoryTypeBits of
non-LINEAR DRM-modifier images; device-local and system memory types stay.
Tegra (sysmem-only, all types device-local) is unchanged.

Not in Mesa main as of fc88667ecb8c (2026-10-15).

--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_image.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_image.c
@@ -1422,6 +1422,29 @@
       }
    }
 
+   /* Fermi..Volta: a CPU map of host-visible VRAM goes through BAR1, and on
+    * these GPUs BAR1 does not return a block-linear DRM-modifier image's
+    * bytes in the modifier's layout, whatever kind the memory carries
+    * (measured on GP104: GPU fill through the image, CPU read back through
+    * BAR1; system memory reads back exactly). The proprietary driver offers
+    * no host-visible VRAM type for such images either (580.178.04 Vulkan on
+    * GP104: memoryTypeBits 0x82, a non-host-visible system type and the
+    * device-local type). Keep device-local and system memory types only.
+    * Turing+ BAR1 reads back exactly and keeps every type.
+    */
+   if (pdev->info.cls_eng3d < TURING_A &&
+       image->vk.tiling == VK_IMAGE_TILING_DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_EXT &&
+       image->vk.drm_format_mod != DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR) {
+      for (uint32_t i = 0; i < pdev->mem_type_count; i++) {
+         const VkMemoryPropertyFlags props = pdev->mem_types[i].propertyFlags;
+         if ((props & VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_DEVICE_LOCAL_BIT) &&
+             (props & VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_VISIBLE_BIT) &&
+             pdev->info.type != NV_DEVICE_TYPE_SOC)
+            memory_types &= ~BITFIELD_BIT(i);
+      }
+      assert(memory_types != 0);
+   }
+
    uint64_t size_B = 0;
    uint32_t align_B = 0;
    if (image->disjoint) {
